---
title: "borrow_val and return_val (Sui Framework: kiosk)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_access: assert self.has_access(cap)
    q_check_access --> q_abort_owner: no access
    q_abort_owner --> [*]: abort ENotOwner
    q_check_access --> q_check_exists: has access
    q_check_exists --> q_abort_exists: !has_item(id)
    q_abort_exists --> [*]: abort EItemNotFound
    q_check_exists --> q_check_listed: item exists
    q_check_listed --> q_abort_listed: is_listed(id)
    q_abort_listed --> [*]: abort EItemIsListed
    q_check_listed --> q_remove: not listed
    q_remove --> q_return_borrow: dof::remove(Item(id)) + Borrow hot potato
    q_return_borrow --> q_use_item: caller uses item externally
    q_use_item --> q_check_return_kiosk: assert object::id(self) == borrow.kiosk_id
    q_check_return_kiosk --> q_check_return_item: assert object::id(item) == borrow.item_id
    q_check_return_item --> q_restore: dof::add(Item(item_id), item)
    q_restore --> [*]: item returned to kiosk

    note right of q_return_borrow
        INV-001: Borrow hot potato ensures item must be returned
        INV-002: item must be returned to same kiosk (kiosk_id check)
        INV-003: same item must be returned (item_id check)
        INV-004: listed items cannot be borrowed mutably
    end note
